# --- Build artifacts ---
foundation
solver
tools/ref/refsolve
*.o
*.obj
*.a

# --- Instructor-only material (NEVER commit to the student repo) ---
# The generator itself (tools/gen) IS shipped -- students need it to make
# practice instances with their own seeds. What stays behind is the secret
# seed, the instances it produces, the design rationale, and -- most
# importantly -- the reference solvers, which are complete working
# implementations of exactly the techniques the assignment asks students to
# find. Publishing tools/ref/solvers would be publishing the answer.
docs/
tools/manifest/hidden.json
checksums/hidden.sha256
instances_hidden/
outputs/
tools/ref/solvers/
tools/discriminate.py
tools/fuzz_solvers.py
# The scoreboard Worker. src/validate.js IS the list of integrity checks;
# shipping it would hand students the exact checks to defeat.
scoreboard/

# --- Per-student / local work ---
solver.cpp
result.json
*.tmp.out

# --- Downloadable tier (distributed via GitHub Releases, not git) ---
# Only the *_dev tier is committed.
instances/*_large.graph
instances/*_large.queries
instances/*_large.answers
instances/*_large.meta.json
instances/*.qplan
instances/*.gz

# --- Tooling ---
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
